			"notes": "Fabric build of StrikerLoad. Needs Fabric API.\n\nWorks on dedicated servers, in **single-player**, and on a LAN\nhost. Other players do not need the mod - everything it spawns is\nvanilla, so unmodified clients can join and see it all.\n\n## Which jar do I download?\n\n| Your server version | Download the jar ending in |\n|---|---|\n| Minecraft 26.2 | `+mc26.2.jar` |\n| Minecraft 26.1.x | `+mc26.1.2.jar` |\n| Minecraft 1.21.11 | `+mc1.21.11.jar` |\n\nThese go in `mods/`, not `plugins/`. There is one jar per\nMinecraft generation and they are **not** interchangeable.\n\nPlaying single-player? Load the world with **Allow Cheats on** -\nthat is the only way to reach `/strikerload give`, and without it\nthere is no way to get a payload item.\n\nTwo things that differ from the Paper plugin: permissions gate on\nvanilla **operator level** rather than the plugin's\n`strikerload.use.*` nodes, and config is JSON at\n`config/strikerload.json`. Both are covered in\n`strikerload-fabric/README.md`.\n\nBuilt by GitHub Actions from 7c1182941c12c1dc8e92298254418f8482b5f113.\n\nVerify what you downloaded matches what was built from this source:\n\n```\nsha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt\n```\n\nBuild log: https://github.com/creeperdiamonds/strikerload/actions/runs/34894766976\n\nLicensed AGPL-3.0-or-later."
		},
